+**Evaluation.** The preserved 553-negative snapshot spans 157 requirements. Their inventory has 1,290 cases: 606 positive and 684 negative. TRF-130's additional 12 cases are separately identified. Individual review states are retained; being in an inventory does not certify a fixture. The six-requirement development core has 37 cases (17 positive, 20 negative), with 20 intended-only repaired counterparts. It is not a representative held-out benchmark. The bundled regression checks use explicitly source-authored reference controls; their passing results do not measure automatic generation or repair quality. Only explicitly hashed historical candidate copies are bundled as offline diagnostic replay inputs; historical output trees remain preserved separately.
 
 The external evaluator reports ordinary agreement, positive acceptance, strict intended detection, unrelated/additional rejection, missed defects, no executable verdict and unresolved attribution separately. Unreviewed violation semantics stay unresolved. Original no-verdict outcomes cannot gain offline credit. Evaluation fixtures, labels and counterparts are never loaded by the generation/repair modules. Approved internal runtime probes contain only schema-derived synthetic empty targets; conformance of those probes is ignored.
 
